Site Folder
The code reads and writes files through site, the site folder. Quarto sets QUARTO_PROJECT_DIR to the site folder during a render. When you run the code by hand, the variable is usually missing. If it is missing or empty, the code looks for _quarto.yml in the current folder and then in the folder above it. It uses the first folder that holds the file. If neither folder holds it, the code stops with an error. So run it from the site folder or from analyses/. Then the code reads _scripts/report.R, which holds the functions that the reports share.

site &lt;- Sys.getenv("QUARTO_PROJECT_DIR")
if (!nzchar(site)) {
  site &lt;- Find(function(dir) file.exists(file.path(dir, "_quarto.yml")), c(".", ".."))
}
if (is.null(site)) {
  stop("Run this code from the site folder or from its analyses/ folder.")
}
source(file.path(site, "_scripts", "report.R"), local = TRUE)

Paper Figures
Save each figure for the paper in figures/, which git tracks and the site publishes. save_png(), from _scripts/report.R, runs a function that draws the plot. For a ggplot p, pass function() print(p). It stops when figures is a link or a file. It draws into a temporary file in figures/. It gives that file its name only when the plot succeeds and the file ends as a whole PNG file does. So a failed plot, or a file cut short, leaves no partial file there.

save_png("bootstrap-means.png", function() {
  hist(boot_means, main = "Bootstrap means of score", xlab = "Mean score")
})
